                "entry_id": "bd21631d-5491-3b8f-bf95-61952b651a8d",
                "word": "antidisestablishmentarianism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0cd73da2-489c-43ec-8523-6996a84e03c9",
                        "entry_id": "bd21631d-5491-3b8f-bf95-61952b651a8d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "antidisestablishmentarianisms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "259ce3a1-d575-3dc7-914f-d7c487380723",
                        "entry_id": "bd21631d-5491-3b8f-bf95-61952b651a8d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A political philosophy opposed to the separation of a religious group (church) and a government (state), especially the belief held by those in 19th-century England opposed to separating the Anglican church from the civil government or to refer to separation of church and state."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7855823a-2011-4b64-896a-ce17b3287165",
                                "sense_id": "259ce3a1-d575-3dc7-914f-d7c487380723",
                                "text": "As we said yesterday, the case for antidisestablishmentarianism has never been more threadbare."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "785a8748-77ec-4251-b4b2-07c36777db9e",
                                "sense_id": "259ce3a1-d575-3dc7-914f-d7c487380723",
                                "text": "Jed Rubenfeld, who actually may not have been recycling a Boerne Court- rejected argument into a law review article,⁴⁵⁰ reasoned that RFRA indeed lacked constitutionality, but because of First Amendment antidisestablishmentarianism, and not the reasons offered by the Court.⁴⁵¹"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91c4c1e0-73b8-4d44-ab36-6467de5f75bd",
                                "sense_id": "259ce3a1-d575-3dc7-914f-d7c487380723",
                                "text": "The establishmentarianism of Hatch's alliance-building strategy undermined by the disestablishmentarianism of Wiglesworth's treachery triggers an antidisestablishmentarianism in Hawk — but the negation of Wiglesworth's 'dis' coupled with the counter-negation of Hawk's 'anti' does not simply generate a synthetic affirmation of Hatch's 'establishmentarianism'. Instead, Hawk's antidisestablishmentarianism, like a cancerous wart on the end of the nose, is perched at the fuzzy border separating ontology from oncology, malignity from malignancy."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
